 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "Process boundary",
   "items": [
    "With use_mcp=True, run_triage spawns python -m ombuds.platform.mcp.server and talks MCP over stdio; the graph can't tell, because both dispatchers satisfy ToolDispatcher",
    "The HTTP routes do not use it: /claims/triage runs tools in-process"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Sync to async bridge",
   "items": [
    "Graph nodes are synchronous; McpToolClient runs an async ClientSession on a background thread through an anyio blocking portal",
    "A tool error comes back as an MCP isError result; the server uses the tool name as the call id"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "Shared state, one wiring",
   "items": [
    "The server builds the same Postgres-backed runtime as the API, so an approval submitted over MCP shows up in /approvals",
    "External clients bypass the agent and its scope: they can reach issue_payment, still behind a human approval, with arguments redacted"
   ]
  }
 ]
